    <id>https://www.nber.org/papers/w35897</id>
    <title>Inverted Gravity</title>
    <updated>2026-10-01T00:00:00+00:00</updated>
    <author>
      <name>James E. Anderson, Mario Larch &amp; Yoto V. Yotov</name>
    </author>
    <content>&lt;b&gt; NBER Working Papers&lt;/b&gt; &lt;br&gt;We invert structural gravity to recover trade cost changes delivering targeted outcomes. For attainable welfare targets, one instrument per target yields a unique solution. At unchanged producer prices and to first order, each instrument must change by the welfare target divided by its own expenditure share; the required domestic change is about the size of the target, while the import change is several times larger. Inverting observed trade flows gives a separate trade cost change for each of the two directions in which a pair of countries trades. Applications to NAFTA and world trade illustrate the benefits of our approach.</content>
